WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.992
"Why Vegans Should Eat
More Plant-Based"

00:00:10.992 --> 00:00:16.440
In the United States, the #1 risk factor
for death is the American diet,

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:19.560
associated with more deaths
than any other risk factor,

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:23.760
responsible for like half a million
mothers, fathers, sisters, brothers,

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:28.770
friends, and family dying every year
because of what they ate,

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:31.440
mostly from cardiovascular disease.

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:35.100
That's where plant-based
diets can come in,

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:38.340
associated with lower risk of
developing cardiovascular disease,

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:41.280
lower risk of dying from
cardiovascular disease,

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:44.400
and, in fact, a lower risk of dying
from all causes put together.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:47.760
Progressively increasing
the intake of plant foods

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:49.920
by reducing the amount
of intake of animal foods

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:52.620
may enable us to live
longer, healthier lives.

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:54.960
And it doesn't take much.

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:58.200
If you look at the largest cohort
study on diet and health in history,

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:03.840
the NIH-AARP study, they found
that replacing just 3% of energy

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:06.600
from animal protein with plant
protein was associated

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:09.840
with a 10% lower overall mortality
in both men and women.

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:13.860
Of all the animal protein sources,
eggs were the worst.

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:18.060
Swapping in 3% plant protein
for egg protein was associated

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:22.967
with twice the benefit, exceeding 20%
lower mortality in men and women.

00:01:22.967 --> 00:01:25.860
The researchers concluded that
the study provides evidence

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:29.160
for public health recommendations
regarding dietary modifications

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:33.840
in terms of choice of protein sources
that may promote health and longevity,

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:37.059
and plant protein is preferable.

00:01:37.059 --> 00:01:39.780
Now, healthy plant-based
diets are associated

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:44.520
with lower risk of all-cause mortality,
but with an emphasis on healthy.

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:47.820
When individuals increase their
consumption of plant foods

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:49.800
while decreasing their
intake of animal foods,

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:54.060
there could be an increase in their
consumption of less-healthy options:

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:57.120
highly processed plant foods
like Coke and Wonder Bread.

00:01:57.120 --> 00:02:00.480
One cannot assume that
simply avoiding animal foods

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:03.660
will necessarily produce
such a healthy diet.

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:08.220
In order to distinguish between
healthful and unhealthful vegan diets,

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:11.400
the term "whole food, plant-based diet"
is attributed

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:14.220
to Cornell Professor Emeritus
in Nutritional Biochemistry,

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:16.080
Dr. T. Colin Campbell.

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:18.780
If you look at India, for example,
you see a decreasing

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:21.120
in whole plant food content
of their diets,

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:23.700
along with increasing
risk of obesity

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:25.800
and noncommunicable
chronic diseases.

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:28.920
This may help explain why
disease rates are on the rise

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:32.400
even in a country with
a large vegetarian contingent.

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:36.240
This may help explain why
health-wise vegans in the US

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:38.460
do better than vegans in the UK.

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:41.820
The #1 reason people in the US
eat plant-based is health,

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:45.840
and so they eat more plants,
more fiber, vitamin C ---

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:48.480
only found concentrated
in whole plant foods.

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:52.860
Whereas the #1 reason given
in the UK is animal welfare reasons,

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:57.900
and so they may be more likely to just
switch over to vegan doughnuts.

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:02.280
You can't know if vegans really
have to eat more plants though

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:05.520
until you put it to the test.

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:09.060
An evaluation of an 8-week
whole food plant-based

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:10.320
lifestyle modification program

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:14.460
in which two dozen were already
eating vegetarian or vegan,

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:16.860
but not necessarily
whole food plant-based.

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:20.880
And after 8 weeks, even
those who already started out

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:24.000
vegetarian or vegan experienced
significant weight loss

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:25.380
and reductions in cholesterol.

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:28.980
They lost ten pounds and dropped
their LDL cholesterol 15 points.

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:33.000
So even a short-term whole food
plant-based dietary intervention

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:34.740
may provide significant benefits

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:38.220
for non-vegetarians, vegetarians,
and vegans alike.

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:42.000
We have a food supply
in which "junk" is a food group,

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:45.420
willfully engineered
to maximize eating for profit,

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:50.820
and the industry will happily make all
the vegan junk we're willing to buy.

00:03:50.820 --> 00:03:54.780
In fact, if you compare the consumption
of ultra-processed junk

00:03:54.780 --> 00:03:58.200
across different eating patterns,
vegetarians and vegans were found

00:03:58.200 --> 00:04:01.301
to be eating the most junk,
like potato chips and cookies.

00:04:01.301 --> 00:04:05.899
Not all plant-based foods exert
the same health effects.

00:04:05.899 --> 00:04:07.651
But what about animal food?

00:04:07.651 --> 00:04:09.480
These researchers
separately scored

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:11.280
the quality of different
plant-based foods

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:13.800
with a plant-based
Diet Quality Index,

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:15.960
and also various animal foods

00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:18.720
in an animal-based
Diet Quality Index.

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:21.540
For example, if you'd consider
processed meats and red meats

00:04:21.540 --> 00:04:23.220
as unhealthy animal foods,

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:26.880
but fish, seafood, dairy, and
poultry as healthy animal foods --

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:29.520
and you throw eggs in
with the unhealthy, too,

00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:31.260
based on the most recent evidence --

00:04:31.260 --> 00:04:33.480
they found that the higher
quality of plant foods,

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:36.300
the longer you live,
the lower all-cause mortality.

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:41.100
But no independent association was
found for the quality of animal foods,

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:45.000
meaning they all seemed just as bad
in terms of cancer mortality,

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:48.701
heart disease mortality,
and all-cause mortality.

00:04:48.701 --> 00:04:52.500
In light of the expanding global
threat of cardiovascular disease,

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:55.860
large-scale shifts toward healthy
plant-based diets are imperative

00:04:55.860 --> 00:04:58.200
to ensure future human health.

00:04:58.200 --> 00:05:03.578
But all plant foods
are not created equal.

